{"key":"apchem-mcq-022","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"[Ar]3d^5","working":"Neutral iron (Z = 26) has the electron configuration [Ar] 3d^6 4s^2. When first-row transition metal atoms ionize, the 4s electrons are lost before the 3d electrons because the 4s electrons have a higher principal quantum number (n = 4). To form the Fe^3+ ion, three electrons are removed: the two 4s electrons are lost first, followed by one 3d electron. This leaves five electrons in the 3d subshell, yielding the ground-state electron configuration [Ar] 3d^5.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":466,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":466,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":390,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":168,"reasoningTokens":222},"totalTokens":856,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":222,"promptTokenCount":466,"candidatesTokenCount":168,"totalTokenCount":856,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":466}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":168}]},"reasoningTokens":222,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3558,"keyed_label":"B"}
