{"key":"apchem-mcq-031","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"B. A metallic solid, such as a transition metal","working":"Metallic solids conduct electricity in both solid and molten states because delocalized valence electrons remain mobile. They are malleable because metal cations can slide past one another without disrupting metallic bonding. Many metals have moderately high melting points, matching the description. Ionic solids conduct when molten but not as solids and are brittle. Covalent network solids like SiO2 are typically nonconducting and brittle. Molecular solids like iodine are nonconducting and low-melting.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":526,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":14,"cacheReadTokens":512},"outputTokens":333,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":131,"reasoningTokens":202},"totalTokens":859,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":526,"completion_tokens":333,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":512,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":14,"total_tokens":859,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":512},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":202}},"reasoningTokens":202,"cachedInputTokens":512},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4400,"keyed_label":"B"}
{"key":"apchem-mcq-037","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"The UV photon has more energy than the IR photon because UV light has a shorter wavelength, which corresponds to a higher frequency, and photon energy is directly proportional to frequency (E = hf).","working":"The energy of a photon is given by Planck's equation, E = hf = hc/λ, where h is Planck's constant, f is frequency, c is the speed of light, and λ is wavelength. UV light has a shorter wavelength and higher frequency than IR light across the electromagnetic spectrum. Because energy is directly proportional to frequency (and inversely proportional to wavelength), a photon of UV light has greater energy than a photon of IR light. Choice A correctly identifies this ranking and justification.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":593,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":593,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":374,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":174,"reasoningTokens":200},"totalTokens":967,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":200,"promptTokenCount":593,"candidatesTokenCount":174,"totalTokenCount":967,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":593}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":174}]},"reasoningTokens":200,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3693,"keyed_label":"A"}
